The number one piece of non-obvious advice that I learned from this group
and that I'd have given myself is "don't gain experience too quickly."

That is to say, try to keep your experience relatively low as you descend
through the first several levels of the dungeon.  Monster difficulty
increases with your experience as well as with dungeon level, so if you
become high level before you find good gear (especially armor), you'll
get slaughtered.  Instead, let your pet handle as much of the combat as
you can manage: it will toughen up and serve as a good bodyguard.  Once
you're deeper in the dungeon and have a good kit, you can jump up in
level.

